POSTHOG_KEY=""
POSTHOG_HOST="https://us.i.posthog.com"
# Client-side key (posthog-js). Use the same project key; NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix
# makes it available to the browser bundle via src/app/providers.tsx.
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=""
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST="https://us.i.posthog.com"

# --- Grafana Cloud telemetry ingestion (src/lib/telemetry/otel.ts) -------------
# Telemetry ships over OTLP/HTTP to the Grafana Cloud stack, using the
# OpenTelemetry standard variable names — which is also what the stack's
# OpenTelemetry tile hands you, so copy from there rather than assembling by hand.
# Grafana Cloud authenticates with Basic, not Bearer, and the tile's token is
# already the base64 credential: do not encode it a second time.
#
# Find the values: Grafana Cloud portal → your stack → OpenTelemetry tile →
# Configure. Create the token as an Access Policy with metrics write (plus logs and
# traces only if the residency decision below changes), not a service-account key.
#
# POSTURE, decided 2026-10-19: METRICS ONLY. This is a DIFC/PDPL product and the
# stack is in Canada East. Metrics are aggregate counters with no customer labels;
# traces and logs from the voice path can carry caller data, so they are given no
# destination at all. Set exactly these two lines:
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS="Authorization=Basic <access-policy token>"
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_METRICS_ENDPOINT="https://otlp-gateway-prod-ca-east-0.grafana.net/otlp/v1/metrics"
#
# Do NOT set OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT. It is the base URL, and every signal
# inherits from it — traces and logs would get a destination by accident, which is
# the decision that was declined. A signal with no endpoint builds no exporter; it
# does not fall back to the SDK's default of http://localhost:4318.
#
# With neither variable set the SDK exports nothing and says why at boot, so an
# unconfigured deployment loses telemetry and not the request path. There is no
# default host to fall back to: a hardcoded ingestion host would ship telemetry
# from a deployment that never configured one.
#
# Only ever widen this with the residency decision re-opened:
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT="https://otlp-gateway-prod-ca-east-0.grafana.net/otlp"
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT=""   # full URL, used exactly as given
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_LOGS_ENDPOINT=""
#
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TIMEOUT="10000"     # per-request timeout, milliseconds
# OTEL_SERVICE_NAME="securevoice-api"
# OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLE_RATE="1"
# OTEL_EXPORT_INTERVAL_MS="60000"
# OTEL_SDK_DISABLED="false"
#
# Log shipping is a separate destination (Axiom, src/lib/telemetry/axiom.ts):
# AXIOM_API_TOKEN / AXIOM_DATASET. Better Stack is not a log-shipping target here.

# Abuse controls (src/lib/abuse/config.ts + bad-actor ladder) ---------------
# All optional; defaults live in the abuse config module. Per-org overrides use
# the ABUSE_ALLOWED_COUNTRIES__<ORG> / ABUSE_PLAN_TIER__<ORG> suffix form.
#
# ABUSE_BUSINESS_HOURS_START/END/TZ double as the PERMITTED CALLING WINDOW for
# routine-category calls (call_category=routine): calls are refused outside it,
# and the dial worker parks them until it opens. For an FCA-style 8am-8pm rule
# set START=8, END=20. Defaults: 6/22 Asia/Dubai.
# ABUSE_ALLOWED_COUNTRIES=""
# ABUSE_DENIED_COUNTRIES=""
# ABUSE_DENIED_PREFIXES=""
# ABUSE_TEST_NUMBERS=""
# ABUSE_BURST_WINDOW_SEC=""
# ABUSE_BURST_RATE_MAX=""
# ABUSE_NEW_PREFIX_WINDOW_SEC=""
# ABUSE_NEW_PREFIX_BURST=""
# ABUSE_AFTER_HOURS_WARN=""
# ABUSE_AFTER_HOURS_PAUSE=""
# ABUSE_BUSINESS_HOURS_START=""
# ABUSE_BUSINESS_HOURS_END=""
# ABUSE_BUSINESS_HOURS_TZ=""
# ABUSE_ATTEMPT_WINDOW_SEC=""
# ABUSE_MAX_ATTEMPTS_PER_ORG=""
# ABUSE_MAX_PREFIXES_PER_ORG=""
# ABUSE_MAX_TRACKED_ORGS=""
# ABUSE_PAUSE_TTL_SEC=""
# ABUSE_COOLDOWN_SEC=""
# ABUSE_ORG_CONCURRENCY_CAP=""
# ABUSE_GLOBAL_CONCURRENCY_CAP=""

